euthydemus-knowing.md:7: argue/readings: S4 is read 2 ways: euthydemus-knowing.logic.r2 has "knows_something → knowing_of_known"; euthydemus-knowing.logic.r2.2 and euthydemus-knowing.logic.r2.3 have nothing from it; they differ when only "you know something" is true, which the second allows
euthydemus-knowing.md:7: argue/answered: S4: answered no, which keeps euthydemus-knowing.logic.r2, to: Suppose "you know something" is true and "you are knowing of the knowledge which you have (Socrates' qualified sense)" is false. Is S4, "Certainly, of the knowledge which I have.", true then?
euthydemus-knowing.md:15: argue/readings: S8 is read 2 ways: euthydemus-knowing.logic.r2 has "ignorant_something → not_knowing_of_unknown"; euthydemus-knowing.logic.r2.2 and euthydemus-knowing.logic.r2.3 have nothing from it; they differ when only "there are things which you do not know" is true, which the second allows
euthydemus-knowing.md:15: argue/answered: S8: answered no, which keeps euthydemus-knowing.logic.r2, to: Suppose "there are things which you do not know" is true and "you are not knowing of that which you do not know (Socrates' qualified sense)" is false. Is S8, "Yes, friend, of that which I do not know.", true then?
